Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Finite-length longitudinal PEEC", "Title",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"c7fc5056-5111-3a4a-bd68-84a3b8036159"],

Cell["\:7f2a\:96e8\:8f69 / Miao Yuxuan \[CenterDot] \:6dee\:5357\:5e08\:8303\
\:5b66\:9662 / Huainan Normal University", "Subtitle",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"310c1330-c563-be43-923b-0c1c7ded63d2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Model, inputs and scope", "Section",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"9a803164-97f6-ff4b-8978-49d6705f820f"],

Cell["Z=R+j\[Omega]L; Zi=V1; 1\:1d40i=It", "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"a61179bc-ba6f-9f40-9612-5e48eb850212"],

Cell["SI; exp(+j omega t); RMS; sigma=58 MS/m; mu_r=1; 20 C", "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"ac1cd0e0-8d44-d147-8c57-e5209573280b"],

Cell["\<\
Change length or cross divisions; compare complex port constraints and power. \
The basis is longitudinal.\
\>", "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"ef654d33-61a7-4d49-90fa-ae41245679b7"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Derivation and interpretation", "Section",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"9bae286b-f530-c94f-b5a7-7b8fafed9d50"],

Cell["\<\
Discretize the cross section into longitudinal current basis elements. \
Galerkin projection of the magnetoquasistatic integral equation gives Z=R+j\
\[Omega]L, where R follows from conductivity and basis overlap and L contains \
finite-length mutual and self interactions.\
\>", "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"d1694da9-df22-9441-9a5b-ee65057f3aa8"],

Cell["\<\
Solve Zi=V1 and 1\:1d40i=It simultaneously. The terminal voltage and complex \
currents are unknowns. Real input power must equal the quadratic resistive \
loss i\:1d34Ri.\
\>", "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"1d846e76-3e81-d24b-9487-8e7f3f503f9c"],

Cell["\<\
Vary cross-section divisions, longitudinal length and quadrature \
independently. This longitudinal basis omits general transverse current and \
end-region charge; it must not be presented as a full vector 3D conductor \
solution.\
\>", "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,ExpressionUUID->"b5e05286-8232-fc4a-bd48-f6cf875f2f3b"],

